# NOTE:
# Private software — a template, not a real list.
#
# Some of what you install says something about you: where you live, who you work for, what you are building, what you 
# are protecting yourself against.
#
# None of that belongs in a public repository, even though it is not a secret in the usual sense.
#
# So this repository keeps a place for it that is never committed.
#
# Copy this file and edit your copy:
#
#     cp Brewfile.optional.example Brewfile.optional
#
# Brewfile.optional is listed in .gitignore, no public file refers to it, and bootstrap never reads it.
#
# Install from it yourself when you want to:
#
#     brew bundle install --file=Brewfile.optional
#
# The entries below are placeholders.
#
# Replace them; do not commit the result.


# cask "<REGION_SPECIFIC_APP>"


# cask "<VPN_OR_SECURITY_TOOL>"


# cask "<WORK_RELATED_APP>"


# cask "<PERSONAL_APP>"


# brew "<PRIVATE_PROJECT_TOOLCHAIN>"


# brew "<WORK_TOOL>"


# brew "<DATABASE_FOR_A_SPECIFIC_PROJECT>"

